00:23:17,819 --> 00:23:21,492
- [Tom] "Why don't I have any friends?"

505
00:23:21,492 --> 00:23:23,974
(vault door slamming)

506
00:23:23,974 --> 00:23:25,808
(beeping)

507
00:23:25,808 --> 00:23:28,234
(mechanical whirring)

508
00:23:28,234 --> 00:23:29,453
(slamming)

509
00:23:29,453 --> 00:23:31,790
(high pitched metallic sound)

510
00:23:31,790 --> 00:23:33,170
(slamming)

511
00:23:33,170 --> 00:23:34,003
- Hey guys.

512
00:23:34,003 --> 00:23:35,489
- Yeah, Mike, you're probably wondering

513
00:23:35,489 --> 00:23:37,191
why I'm pissed off at you.

514
00:23:37,191 --> 00:23:38,024
- Oh!

515
00:23:38,024 --> 00:23:39,299
- Ah, no, not really.

516
00:23:39,299 --> 00:23:40,893
- Well, too bad, I'm going to exact

517
00:23:40,893 --> 00:23:42,744
petty, childish revenge on ya.

518
00:23:42,744 --> 00:23:43,599
- Oh!

519
00:23:43,599 --> 00:23:45,429
- Yeah, and I'm going to have to pour beer

520
00:23:45,429 --> 00:23:46,961
on your most beloved object!

521
00:23:46,961 --> 00:23:49,181
(laughs maniacally)

522
00:23:49,181 --> 00:23:52,394
What is your most beloved
object, if you don't mind?

523
00:23:52,394 --> 00:23:53,295
- Well, I'd have to say,

524
00:23:53,295 --> 00:23:55,855
my personalized heirloom beer stein.

525
00:23:55,855 --> 00:23:57,700
(both laugh)

526
00:23:57,700 --> 00:24:00,983
- Oh, say, could you help
me exact revenge, please?

527
00:24:00,983 --> 00:24:03,173
- Oh no, please, Crow, no, uh, sure.

528
00:24:03,173 --> 00:24:05,330
- Okay, okay, nice and easy like.

529
00:24:05,330 --> 00:24:06,163
- Alright.

530
00:24:06,163 --> 00:24:07,370
- Yeah, take the beer there, that's right.

531
00:24:07,370 --> 00:24:08,837
And pour it all over your stein!

532
00:24:08,837 --> 00:24:11,431
(cackles)

533
00:24:11,431 --> 00:24:12,264
That's right, you're going to get

534
00:24:12,264 --> 00:24:13,999
what you got coming, Mr. Cool!

535
00:24:13,999 --> 00:24:16,599
Teach you a lesson in a big way!

536
00:24:16,599 --> 00:24:18,559
- But Crow, you're out of your mind,

537
00:24:18,559 --> 00:24:20,881
don't you know he'll kill you for that?

538
00:24:20,881 --> 00:24:22,830
- Ah, don't worry your pretty
little head about it, Serbo.

539
00:24:22,830 --> 00:24:23,663
- Oh!

540
00:24:23,663 --> 00:24:24,526
- Hey, you know, Crow, I should tell you,

541
00:24:24,526 --> 00:24:27,271
that you are most beloved
to me, too, you know that?

542
00:24:27,271 --> 00:24:29,680
- Okay then, buddy, you
are going to take that beer

543
00:24:29,680 --> 00:24:30,979
and throw it on me!

544
00:24:30,979 --> 00:24:32,162
- But Crow!
- [Tom] Oh!

545
00:24:32,162 --> 00:24:32,995
- Do it!

546
00:24:32,995 --> 00:24:34,176
Yeah, that's right loser!

547
00:24:34,176 --> 00:24:37,593
You know you got it comin', there you go.

548
00:24:38,788 --> 00:24:40,373
Revenge is sweet!

549
00:24:40,373 --> 00:24:41,614
- Okay, now get out of here, you punk,

550
00:24:41,614 --> 00:24:42,965
and take your damn beer with you.

551
00:24:42,965 --> 00:24:45,127
- Okay, alright, well, I
think I learned my lesson.

552
00:24:45,127 --> 00:24:46,294
See you, Crow.

553
00:24:47,375 --> 00:24:49,045
(laughs maniacally)

554
00:24:49,045 --> 00:24:51,618
(laughing peters out)

555
00:24:51,618 --> 00:24:53,702
- You know, that didn't pan
out quite the way I expected.

556
00:24:53,702 --> 00:24:54,535
- Oh.

557
00:24:56,621 --> 00:25:00,788
(Mystery Science Theater 3000 Theme)

558
00:25:02,781 --> 00:25:05,784
- [Mike] Ah, it's good beer.

559
00:25:05,784 --> 00:25:06,898
- I'm sorry.

560
00:25:06,898 --> 00:25:10,405
- [Tom] "I didn't mean to turn you on."

561
00:25:10,405 --> 00:25:11,949
- Well I said I was sorry!

562
00:25:11,949 --> 00:25:15,949
- [Mike] "Look, I'm really
remorseful, you cow!"

563
00:25:17,620 --> 00:25:19,370
- Well say something!

564
00:25:21,305 --> 00:25:22,857
- I guess I was just tired.

565
00:25:22,857 --> 00:25:23,690
- [Crow] That's why I didn't really

566
00:25:23,690 --> 00:25:26,529
do anything to make you mad.

567
00:25:26,529 --> 00:25:27,409
- Come here.

568
00:25:27,409 --> 00:25:31,576
- [Tom] I need you to help me
shift the turbo hydromatic.

569
00:25:34,481 --> 00:25:37,481
- [Mike] "Okay, you can sex me now."

570
00:25:44,457 --> 00:25:47,413
- [Crow] Ooh, he slips off the babushka.

571
00:25:47,413 --> 00:25:50,080
- [Tom] Ooh, next comes the wig.

572
00:25:53,436 --> 00:25:57,519
- [Mike] "Please accept
my tongue as an apology."

573
00:26:02,672 --> 00:26:03,505
- [Crow] "Wait a minute,

574
00:26:03,505 --> 00:26:06,012
one of your spacers fell out again."

575
00:26:06,012 --> 00:26:10,713
- [Tom] Oh wait, it was a dream,
he's kissing his Budweiser.

576
00:26:10,713 --> 00:26:14,637
- [Mike] Nope, forget
that scene, never mind.

577
00:26:14,637 --> 00:26:16,579
- [Crow] He should be showing more leg.

578
00:26:16,579 --> 00:26:19,291
- [Mike] Yeah, someone
else's leg, I think.

579
00:26:19,291 --> 00:26:20,888
- [Tom] Uh-oh.

580
00:26:20,888 --> 00:26:22,318
- Hey, recognize him?

581
00:26:22,318 --> 00:26:26,217
- Of course I do, he's the
guy with all the words.

582
00:26:26,217 --> 00:26:28,847
- You mean he's the
guy with all the bread.

583
00:26:28,847 --> 00:26:30,008
Come on, let's go pick him up.

584
00:26:30,008 --> 00:26:30,841
- [Tom] Words, bread.

585
00:26:30,841 --> 00:26:34,091
Must be Samuel Johnson with a baguette.

586
00:26:40,277 --> 00:26:41,864
- The good Samaritans, I presume.

587
00:26:41,864 --> 00:26:42,826
- Need help?

588
00:26:42,826 --> 00:26:44,368
- Yeah, I guess you could say so.

589
00:26:44,368 --> 00:26:46,907
Traveler here, my bike
seems to have thrown a rock.

590
00:26:46,907 --> 00:26:48,170
- Well now, seems to me,

591
00:26:48,170 --> 00:26:50,753
you've got an awful lot of
trouble with that wreck.

592
00:26:50,753 --> 00:26:52,867
Yesterday, you had it on a truck bed.

593
00:26:52,867 --> 00:26:56,345
- Oh, yeah, we've met before, haven't we?

594
00:26:56,345 --> 00:26:59,208
- Why you, my fair lady, you're Guinevere.

595
00:26:59,208 --> 00:27:01,324
But I don't seem to recall your name, sir.

596
00:27:01,324 --> 00:27:02,713
- Look, cut the bologna out, huh?

597
00:27:02,713 --> 00:27:03,770
You want a ride?

598
00:27:03,770 --> 00:27:06,431
- My other name is Michelle, he's Buzz.

599
00:27:06,431 --> 00:27:07,710
- Michelle and Buzz.

600
00:27:07,710 --> 00:27:08,543
- [Mike] I'll allow it.

601
00:27:08,543 --> 00:27:09,376
- Mine's Critter.

602
00:27:09,376 --> 00:27:10,353
- Critter?

603
00:27:10,353 --> 00:27:12,034
- Yeah, you know, like a cowboy's horse,

604
00:27:12,034 --> 00:27:14,012
or a wayward cat without a home.

605
00:27:14,012 --> 00:27:15,808
- Look, come on, you want a ride?

606
00:27:15,808 --> 00:27:16,970
- Yes, we do.

607
00:27:16,970 --> 00:27:17,902
- What do you mean we?

608
00:27:17,902 --> 00:27:20,099
- Well, Traveler and I.

609
00:27:20,099 --> 00:27:22,568
- Look, wise guy, I ain't
carrying no beat up old motorcycle

610
00:27:22,568 --> 00:27:24,186
in the back of my car.

611
00:27:24,186 --> 00:27:26,064
- You won't have to, I got a tow bar.

612
00:27:26,064 --> 00:27:28,095
- No, you gotta have a bumper
hitch for one of them to work.

613
00:27:28,095 --> 00:27:32,015
- It just so happens I
have one of those, too.

614
00:27:32,015 --> 00:27:33,381
- [Tom] "You know, in
fact, I have a car, too,

615
00:27:33,381 --> 00:27:36,048
so I guess I don't need a ride."

616
00:27:37,553 --> 00:27:41,709
- [Crow] Three hours and
four bumpers later...

617
00:27:41,709 --> 00:27:42,644
- [Tom] "We'll take the sidewalk

618
00:27:42,644 --> 00:27:45,061
for another couple of miles."

619
00:27:47,815 --> 00:27:51,232
- [Mike] Oh no, they picked up Joan Baez!

620
00:27:52,996 --> 00:27:56,677
- [Crow] Is there a papoose
tied to the motorcycle?

621
00:27:56,677 --> 00:27:58,970
- You know, I can't get over your name.

622
00:27:58,970 --> 00:28:00,556
It's a funny name, Critter.

623
00:28:00,556 --> 00:28:02,233
- The fellas gave me that
name when I was in preschool.

624
00:28:02,233 --> 00:28:03,271
- [Tom] "I'm back!"

625
00:28:03,271 --> 00:28:05,218
- Yeah, you know, it's
been leading into that.

626
00:28:05,218 --> 00:28:07,468
I held the name since that.

627
00:28:08,646 --> 00:28:10,678
- Yeah, you're kidding.

628
00:28:10,678 --> 00:28:12,278
- [Mike] "Anybody notice
that I'm here now?"

629
00:28:12,278 --> 00:28:15,190
- I'll bet you've got a college education.

630
00:28:15,190 --> 00:28:16,773
- Well, yes and no.

631
00:28:17,749 --> 00:28:18,898
I didn't get a degree,

632
00:28:18,898 --> 00:28:22,120
but I tried my hand at
Colombia and Berkeley.

633
00:28:22,120 --> 00:28:23,637
- Wish I could have gone to one of them.

634
00:28:23,637 --> 00:28:26,669
- [Crow] "Come on, I just
teleported here, it's impressive!"

635
00:28:26,669 --> 00:28:27,502
- Look, I hate to butt in

636
00:28:27,502 --> 00:28:28,869
on this real brilliant conversation,

637
00:28:28,869 --> 00:28:30,711
but we gotta bang it outta here.

638
00:28:30,711 --> 00:28:32,710
Waitress, check please.

639
00:28:32,710 --> 00:28:34,219
Now how 'bout it, Critter, old pal,

640
00:28:34,219 --> 00:28:36,684
seems to me this place
oughta have change for a 50.

641
00:28:36,684 --> 00:28:38,851
Maybe even a hundred, huh?

642
00:28:39,732 --> 00:28:40,565
- [Mike] "Three waters,

643
00:28:40,565 --> 00:28:43,898
those little fish shaped soup crackers."

644
00:28:45,743 --> 00:28:47,993
- [Mike] "I'm an icky elf."

645
00:28:50,531 --> 00:28:52,826
- Ever since I got back, I've
been carrying my billfull,

646
00:28:52,826 --> 00:28:54,254
full of Nepalese money."

647
00:28:54,254 --> 00:28:55,949
- [Crow] From the land of Nipple.

648
00:28:55,949 --> 00:28:59,136
- But you can try to get
it cashed, if you like.

649
00:28:59,136 --> 00:29:03,136
- [Tom] "You tell funny
foreign currency jokes."

650
00:29:04,288 --> 00:29:06,780
- [Mike] "I'm critter, uh-huh."

651
00:29:06,780 --> 00:29:08,553
- Okay, baby, shell out yours.

652
00:29:08,553 --> 00:29:09,886
- [Crow] "Here?"

653
00:29:13,512 --> 00:29:15,580
- [Mike] Well your money's from Senegal.

654
00:29:15,580 --> 00:29:17,763
- 10 bucks, that's all you've got?

655
00:29:17,763 --> 00:29:19,594
- [Michelle] I had to buy gas last night.

656
00:29:19,594 --> 00:29:21,183
- But you went back to the cash register.

657
00:29:21,183 --> 00:29:22,795
- And took what was coming to me.

658
00:29:22,795 --> 00:29:25,450
It amounted to 14 dollars.

659
00:29:25,450 --> 00:29:27,218
- Well, that's just great.

660
00:29:27,218 --> 00:29:29,316
- [Tom] You didn't have to take out FICA.

661
00:29:29,316 --> 00:29:30,789
- With this tab coming to $4.50,

662
00:29:30,789 --> 00:29:33,621
that'll leave us a lousy
$5.50 to get to LA.

663
00:29:33,621 --> 00:29:34,991
- Look, I didn't take anymore

664
00:29:34,991 --> 00:29:37,928
from the cash register than 14 dollars.

665
00:29:37,928 --> 00:29:39,908
That was mine.

666
00:29:39,908 --> 00:29:43,155
- [Mike] "That was my yearly salary."

667
00:29:43,155 --> 00:29:45,478
- Okay, Yak Boy, can you
take care of your own share?

668
00:29:45,478 --> 00:29:46,408
- Yeah.

669
00:29:46,408 --> 00:29:47,794
- [Crow] Natural born cheapskates.

670
00:29:47,794 --> 00:29:50,859
- I can come up with my own share.

671
00:29:50,859 --> 00:29:52,691
- [Tom] "Here's some Guatemalan quetzel."

672
00:29:52,691 --> 00:29:55,713
- And 15 dollars more, to boot.

673
00:29:55,713 --> 00:30:00,470
Why, we oughta be able to reach
Los Angeles with 20 bucks.

674
00:30:00,470 --> 00:30:01,303
- Come on.

675
00:30:02,326 --> 00:30:03,159
- [Tom] "Let's get some of those

676
00:30:03,159 --> 00:30:06,742
pillowy little mints
at the cash register."

677
00:30:09,857 --> 00:30:10,690
- [Mike] "Well, I should get

678
00:30:10,690 --> 00:30:13,857
a little to-go box for my butter pat."

679
00:30:16,482 --> 00:30:20,649
- [Tom] He yanked the engine
off a Kitchen-Aid blender.

680
00:30:23,061 --> 00:30:23,985
- [Crow] Ah!

681
00:30:23,985 --> 00:30:28,597
They're throwing us violently
into the next scene!

682
00:30:28,597 --> 00:30:31,680
- [Tom] "Uh, can I be in your movie?"

683
00:30:35,126 --> 00:30:39,128
- [Mike] "This makes me want
to throw hard candy at people."

684
00:30:39,128 --> 00:30:43,295
- [Crow] So they blew the 15
bucks on a dune buggy rental.

685
00:30:47,066 --> 00:30:50,149
- [Tom] "We're thinking of adopting."

686
00:30:53,302 --> 00:30:55,635
New motorized beach bathtub.

687
00:30:58,471 --> 00:31:00,804
- [Crow] And the movie ends.

688
00:31:02,955 --> 00:31:07,122
- [Tom] "Let's drive through
the oil-soaked ducks again!"

689
00:31:09,890 --> 00:31:13,372
- [Mike] Well, apparently the
story is none of our business.

690
00:31:13,372 --> 00:31:14,539
- What a ride!

691
00:31:15,956 --> 00:31:17,245
- Hey, you wanna go for a ride?

692
00:31:17,245 --> 00:31:18,781
- No, I guess I'll pass for now.

693
00:31:18,781 --> 00:31:20,214
Thanks a lot.

694
00:31:20,214 --> 00:31:21,828
- Well, I don't know about you guys, but--

695
00:31:21,828 --> 00:31:22,966
- [Crow] "I'm an icky elf."

696
00:31:22,966 --> 00:31:24,342
- I'm thirsty.

697
00:31:24,342 --> 00:31:25,527
- [Tom] "So long, odd acquaintance

698
00:31:25,527 --> 00:31:29,694
who inexplicably gave us
rides in your dune buggy.

699
00:31:30,688 --> 00:31:31,577
- [Buzz] There goes--

700
00:31:31,577 --> 00:31:32,906
- [Tom] You can say that a--

701
00:31:32,906 --> 00:31:34,073
- [Crow] One--

702
00:31:35,489 --> 00:31:37,453
- You and Buzz plan to get married in LA?

703
00:31:37,453 --> 00:31:40,132
- [Tom] "You don't need
to spell in front of me."

704
00:31:40,132 --> 00:31:43,287
- I'm riding with him to LA.

705
00:31:43,287 --> 00:31:45,375
He's going to help me
get started as a dancer.

706
00:31:45,375 --> 00:31:46,709
His sister can help me.

707
00:31:46,709 --> 00:31:49,084
That's all there is to it.

708
00:31:49,084 --> 00:31:51,585
- Well, my naive country
girl, I hope it's that simple.

709
00:31:51,585 --> 00:31:52,418
- [Crow] "Uh-huh.

710
00:31:52,418 --> 00:31:53,560
I'm gonna be a dancer!"

711
00:31:53,560 --> 00:31:55,694
- Maybe Buzz does seem a
little bit crude, at times,

712
00:31:55,694 --> 00:31:57,314
but you just have to get to know him.

713
00:31:57,314 --> 00:31:58,969
- [Mike] "It helps if you
meet the other elves."

714
00:31:58,969 --> 00:32:00,386
- Like, two days?

715
00:32:01,968 --> 00:32:02,801
Hey.

716
00:32:02,801 --> 00:32:04,117
- [Tom] "My name's Critter."

717
00:32:04,117 --> 00:32:05,771
- Don't pay attention to me.

718
00:32:05,771 --> 00:32:07,175
What you do is your own business,

719
00:32:07,175 --> 00:32:09,340
and it's really no concern of mine.

720
00:32:09,340 --> 00:32:12,564
- That's right, it is no concern of yours.

721
00:32:12,564 --> 00:32:16,317
I'm going to become a
dancer, Critter, a good one.

722
00:32:16,317 --> 00:32:18,527
I just don't look pretty,

723
00:32:18,527 --> 00:32:20,610
I'm good at dancing, too.

724
00:32:21,459 --> 00:32:24,459
- [Crow] Compared to Steven Hawking.

725
00:32:25,529 --> 00:32:26,765
- Critter stop teasing me,

726
00:32:26,765 --> 00:32:29,435
I want you to take me seriously, for once.

727
00:32:29,435 --> 00:32:31,481
- [Tom] "Okay, little numby head."

728
00:32:31,481 --> 00:32:34,463
- I'm taking this seriously.

729
00:32:34,463 --> 00:32:35,389
- [Crow] "Thank you.

730
00:32:35,389 --> 00:32:37,575
Anyway, what I was
saying about dancing is,

731
00:32:37,575 --> 00:32:40,158
when you dance, mmf mmf mf mf."

732
00:32:42,592 --> 00:32:45,146
- [Tom] "Hey, he's mine,
take your hands off him."

733
00:32:45,146 --> 00:32:46,063
- Get lost!

734
00:32:49,554 --> 00:32:50,942
- Stop it Buzz!

735
00:32:50,942 --> 00:32:52,445
- [Crow] "I'm having Critter's varmint!"

736
00:32:52,445 --> 00:32:53,617
- Listen, yo.

737
00:32:53,617 --> 00:32:56,385
You stay away from Michelle, understand?

738
00:32:56,385 --> 00:32:59,694
- Why don't you let her decide then?

739
00:32:59,694 --> 00:33:00,527
- Nyech.

740
00:33:00,527 --> 00:33:01,707
- [Tom] "Nyech."

741
00:33:01,707 --> 00:33:02,540
- Why not?

742
00:33:03,609 --> 00:33:05,776
Now you're here in California
to play for the act

743
00:33:05,776 --> 00:33:08,505
while his broken down old motorcycle,

744
00:33:08,505 --> 00:33:10,201
or are you here for a reason?

745
00:33:10,201 --> 00:33:11,701
Now, you tell him.

746
00:33:13,418 --> 00:33:14,251
Tell him!

747
00:33:14,251 --> 00:33:16,829
- [Tom] "I'm allergic to shellfish!"

748
00:33:16,829 --> 00:33:18,478
- I'm here to be a dancer!

749
00:33:18,478 --> 00:33:21,978
- [Crow] "I'm going into voice work, too."

750
00:33:23,015 --> 00:33:26,765
- [Mike] Well now the
whole picnic is ruined.

751
00:33:28,191 --> 00:33:29,915
- [Tom] "I'm a crummy critter."

752
00:33:29,915 --> 00:33:34,082
