Go on.

1243
00:56:39,143 --> 00:56:42,726
- [Mike] Aw, geez, she
sat in the clam dip.

1244
00:56:44,641 --> 00:56:48,808
- [Tom] Hey, do you know (bongo babble)?

1245
00:56:49,740 --> 00:56:53,907
- [Crow] "Oh, my goodness,
she's hepped up on the drugs."

1246
00:56:58,785 --> 00:57:02,285
- [Tom] Dancing for Adlai Stevenson there.

1247
00:57:06,169 --> 00:57:10,531
- [Mike] Makes Elaine Benes
look like a good dancer.

1248
00:57:10,531 --> 00:57:13,371
- [Tom] "Thanks, that's most exciting."

1249
00:57:13,371 --> 00:57:15,454
- [Mike] "I'm over here."

1250
00:57:19,258 --> 00:57:22,008
- [Tom] "Whatever, white people."

1251
00:57:26,061 --> 00:57:29,426
- [Crow] When "sexy" becomes "annoying."

1252
00:57:29,426 --> 00:57:32,774
(Tom laughs goofily)

1253
00:57:32,774 --> 00:57:36,941
- [Mike] Yeah, sure, it's fun,
'til someone loses an eye.

1254
00:57:37,805 --> 00:57:41,638
- [Crow] Next, Kitty
Carlisle will read 'Howl.

1255
00:57:43,465 --> 00:57:48,396
- [Tom] "Yeah, yeah, yeah,
right, right, uh-huh, yeah."

1256
00:57:48,396 --> 00:57:49,817
Yeah.

1257
00:57:49,817 --> 00:57:53,567
- [Crow] Hey, that's
her Gore-Tex winter bra.

1258
00:57:56,148 --> 00:58:00,148
- [Tom] Oh, yeah, you're
worth some steam, baby.

1259
00:58:03,095 --> 00:58:05,928
- [Mike] "I should wear a bikini."

1260
00:58:09,280 --> 00:58:13,113
My mom's car parties
used to end up like this.

1261
00:58:14,287 --> 00:58:17,106
♫ I keep your gold boots movin' ♫

1262
00:58:17,106 --> 00:58:20,017
♫ Or your silver ones, we
don't mean to discriminate

1263
00:58:20,017 --> 00:58:23,404
♫ Against the other color boots, hoo ♫

1264
00:58:23,404 --> 00:58:26,591
♫ I keep your gold boots movin', yeah

1265
00:58:26,591 --> 00:58:28,390
- [Crow] Do the wounded turkey!

1266
00:58:28,390 --> 00:58:30,557
(gobbles)

1267
00:58:33,202 --> 00:58:34,667
- [Tom] Boy, I'm glad Oliver
Platt didn't get this role.

1268
00:58:34,667 --> 00:58:35,834
- [Mike] Yeah.

1269
00:58:40,338 --> 00:58:44,371
You know, now it's kind of
like vaguely sexual wallpaper.

1270
00:58:44,371 --> 00:58:45,731
(crowd cheers)

1271
00:58:45,731 --> 00:58:49,898
- [Crow] "I couldn't possibly
go farther in show business!"

1272
00:58:52,262 --> 00:58:54,138
- [Mike] "Thank you, I
hope that in my small way,

1273
00:58:54,138 --> 00:58:56,145
I kept my gold boots moving.

1274
00:58:56,145 --> 00:58:57,341
Thank you.

1275
00:58:57,341 --> 00:58:58,258
Thank you."

1276
00:59:00,440 --> 00:59:01,523
- Well, well.

1277
00:59:02,401 --> 00:59:04,559
Glad to see somebody made it.

1278
00:59:04,559 --> 00:59:07,547
You know, I hate doing
business with leery people,

1279
00:59:07,547 --> 00:59:09,143
like Marty, you know what I mean?

1280
00:59:09,143 --> 00:59:11,948
That's how people get popped.

1281
00:59:11,948 --> 00:59:13,174
- [Crow] Arafat in the 60's.

1282
00:59:13,174 --> 00:59:14,479
- Where's the junk?

1283
00:59:14,479 --> 00:59:16,930
- Relax, live a little bit.

1284
00:59:16,930 --> 00:59:20,211
I mean, what's the use
passing all this bread

1285
00:59:20,211 --> 00:59:22,801
if we can't have fun, right, baby?

1286
00:59:22,801 --> 00:59:25,672
- [Mike] (laughs) We're hippies.

1287
00:59:25,672 --> 00:59:28,820
- You know, for a loose
cat, you sure learn it fast.

1288
00:59:28,820 --> 00:59:32,470
- [Crow] (giggles) Pushing's fun!

1289
00:59:32,470 --> 00:59:34,222
- The money first, huh?

1290
00:59:34,222 --> 00:59:36,392
- What's the matter,
don't you trust me, Buzzy?

1291
00:59:36,392 --> 00:59:37,549
- [Tom] He's Ruth Buzzi?

1292
00:59:37,549 --> 00:59:41,413
- I wouldn't trust you
with a care package.

1293
00:59:41,413 --> 00:59:42,941
- [Crow] "Well, it's sweaty,

1294
00:59:42,941 --> 00:59:45,691
and it's got Cruex on it, but..."

1295
00:59:48,189 --> 00:59:49,189
- Hey, Joey.

1296
00:59:50,933 --> 00:59:52,947
Why don't you look at the tire, huh?

1297
00:59:52,947 --> 00:59:54,318
- [Mike] "Sure, I enjoy a good radial,

1298
00:59:54,318 --> 00:59:56,401
as much as the next guy."

1299
00:59:57,820 --> 01:00:02,460
- [Tom] "Yeah, this thing is
coated with squirrel guts."

1300
01:00:02,460 --> 01:00:05,377
- Okay, see you next Friday, Buzzy.

1301
01:00:07,397 --> 01:00:09,329
Second and Maine, don't forget.

1302
01:00:09,329 --> 01:00:10,675
2pm?

1303
01:00:10,675 --> 01:00:12,007
Okay, baby.

1304
01:00:12,007 --> 01:00:13,655
See you later, Buzzy.

1305
01:00:13,655 --> 01:00:14,825
- [Crow] Oh, I hope he comes

1306
01:00:14,825 --> 01:00:18,064
to the pusher's Christmas party.

1307
01:00:18,064 --> 01:00:19,920
- [Tom] "I take pride in
knowing I provide the kids

1308
01:00:19,920 --> 01:00:22,920
quality drugs at reasonable prices."

1309
01:00:28,660 --> 01:00:32,764
- [Mike] "Excuse me, young
fellow, can I get a fix?"

1310
01:00:32,764 --> 01:00:34,938
(Cartoony chase music)

1311
01:00:34,938 --> 01:00:36,127
- [Tom] "Really, I'm very strung out

1312
01:00:36,127 --> 01:00:39,627
and in need of some Mary Jane, or reefer."

1313
01:00:42,756 --> 01:00:45,589
- [Crow] Slipping on filth is fun!

1314
01:00:48,268 --> 01:00:52,435
- [Mike] "Thought you could
break up with me, huh?"

1315
01:00:54,320 --> 01:00:58,403
- [Crow] "Please, don't
explain my SARSEP to me!"

1316
01:01:01,347 --> 01:01:03,764
- [Tom] It's The Tab Hunters!

1317
01:01:06,811 --> 01:01:11,035
(mismatched guitar sounds)

1318
01:01:11,035 --> 01:01:12,631
- [Crow] "Do you guys ever
notice those girls in front of us

1319
01:01:12,631 --> 01:01:13,869
when we play, what's that about?"

1320
01:01:13,869 --> 01:01:15,057
- Hey man, hold it.

1321
01:01:15,057 --> 01:01:15,954
- [Mike] Hey, someone's taking

1322
01:01:15,954 --> 01:01:17,928
Schmidt guitar lessons back there.

1323
01:01:17,928 --> 01:01:19,207
- Who's that?

1324
01:01:19,207 --> 01:01:20,797
- I don't know, but I like it.

1325
01:01:20,797 --> 01:01:21,817
- [Crow] Look at these hippies.

1326
01:01:21,817 --> 01:01:22,984
Get a haircut!

1327
01:01:26,843 --> 01:01:28,609
- [Tom] "I keep missing the strings."

1328
01:01:28,609 --> 01:01:29,480
- Hi.

1329
01:01:29,480 --> 01:01:31,049
- Hello.

1330
01:01:31,049 --> 01:01:32,050
- I was just listening in.

1331
01:01:32,050 --> 01:01:33,176
What's the name of that tune?

1332
01:01:33,176 --> 01:01:34,312
- [Mike] I call it "Lousy."

1333
01:01:34,312 --> 01:01:36,263
- Doesn't really have a name yet.

1334
01:01:36,263 --> 01:01:37,395
I've been thinking about calling it:

1335
01:01:37,395 --> 01:01:38,870
Do You Wanna Laugh or Cry?

1336
01:01:38,870 --> 01:01:40,146
- Oh, it's one of yours?

1337
01:01:40,146 --> 01:01:42,271
I liked it, that's a good sound.

1338
01:01:42,271 --> 01:01:43,748
- Oh, I'm Chris Howard.

1339
01:01:43,748 --> 01:01:44,635
- [Tom] Who cares?

1340
01:01:44,635 --> 01:01:45,743
- Critter Jones.

1341
01:01:45,743 --> 01:01:47,514
- You have this thing written down?

1342
01:01:47,514 --> 01:01:48,695
- Just the words.

1343
01:01:48,695 --> 01:01:50,764
Never dreamed anyone
else would wanna play it.

1344
01:01:50,764 --> 01:01:51,779
- Well, why don't you come out front,

1345
01:01:51,779 --> 01:01:53,290
let's give it to the guys.

1346
01:01:53,290 --> 01:01:55,831
I'd like to see what they
could do with it, okay?

1347
01:01:55,831 --> 01:01:56,704
- Sure.

1348
01:01:56,704 --> 01:01:58,331
- [Tom] I really enjoyed that one bar.

1349
01:01:58,331 --> 01:02:00,537
- [Chris] Do you have any more of those?

1350
01:02:00,537 --> 01:02:02,067
- Yeah, I got a bunch lyin' around.

1351
01:02:02,067 --> 01:02:03,341
- [Mike] "Great, 'cos
we may wanna burn 'em,

1352
01:02:03,341 --> 01:02:04,311
or crap on 'em, or something."

1353
01:02:04,311 --> 01:02:05,144
(band plays Do You Wanna Laugh or Cry)

1354
01:02:05,144 --> 01:02:08,735
♫ Sounds of former meaning

1355
01:02:08,735 --> 01:02:11,787
- [Crow] Hey, My Three Sons
grew up and started a band.

1356
01:02:11,787 --> 01:02:14,829
And hired two other guys, I guess.

1357
01:02:14,829 --> 01:02:15,987
♫ Wonder why

1358
01:02:15,987 --> 01:02:20,021
- [Mike] Kevin Spacey and
William Holden enjoy the show.

1359
01:02:20,021 --> 01:02:23,771
- [Tom] "One-ee and-a
two-ee, and, oh, damn."

1360
01:02:28,481 --> 01:02:29,939
- [Crow] No, no, it's not working,

1361
01:02:29,939 --> 01:02:34,106
maybe what I heard this morning
was the furnace kicking in."

1362
01:02:36,830 --> 01:02:41,227
♫ Do you want to laugh or cry ♫

1363
01:02:41,227 --> 01:02:43,594
♫ Or look like John Tesh ♫

1364
01:02:43,594 --> 01:02:45,802
- If you gentlemen will excuse me.

1365
01:02:45,802 --> 01:02:48,090
- Oh, you don't have to go yet, baby.

1366
01:02:48,090 --> 01:02:50,091
- Yes, I have to get
changed for my next show.

1367
01:02:50,091 --> 01:02:51,366
- Don't be too long.

1368
01:02:51,366 --> 01:02:55,533
(Mystery Science Theater 3000 Theme)

1369
01:02:57,238 --> 01:02:59,544
- [Tom] "Man, who wrote that
turd of a song out there?

1370
01:02:59,544 --> 01:03:00,893
P.U."

1371
01:03:00,893 --> 01:03:02,915
- Now I won't have to say
goodbye to you in a note.

1372
01:03:02,915 --> 01:03:05,359
- [Mike] "I can say it
in semaphore flags."

1373
01:03:05,359 --> 01:03:08,483
- Are you really leaving
this time, Critter?

1374
01:03:08,483 --> 01:03:09,316
- Yes.

1375
01:03:09,316 --> 01:03:10,243
- [Crow] "As soon as I finish

1376
01:03:10,243 --> 01:03:11,884
my sculpture of Devil's Tower."

1377
01:03:11,884 --> 01:03:13,596
- If you took a good look around you,

1378
01:03:13,596 --> 01:03:14,846
you would, too.

1379
01:03:16,423 --> 01:03:17,772
Close the door.

1380
01:03:17,772 --> 01:03:20,939
- [Mike] "Be on the other side of it."

1381
01:03:23,571 --> 01:03:24,768
- Now sit down.

1382
01:03:24,768 --> 01:03:25,892
- [Mike] "You've probably
never done it before,

1383
01:03:25,892 --> 01:03:27,892
so let me show you how."

1384
01:03:29,322 --> 01:03:30,995
- Leo deals in narcotics.

1385
01:03:30,995 --> 01:03:32,891
LSD, and you name it.

1386
01:03:32,891 --> 01:03:34,682
And Buzz is up to here in it with him.

1387
01:03:34,682 --> 01:03:35,936
- So?

1388
01:03:35,936 --> 01:03:38,753
- [Tom] "I think they should
expand into angel dust."

1389
01:03:38,753 --> 01:03:41,414
- I sold a couple of songs
today, for a hundred bucks.

1390
01:03:41,414 --> 01:03:42,481
You can have half.

1391
01:03:42,481 --> 01:03:46,148
- [Crow] "Some guy paid
me to destroy them."

1392
01:03:46,148 --> 01:03:47,398
- 50 dollars...

1393
01:03:48,776 --> 01:03:51,243
It's more than anyone else has offered me.

1394
01:03:51,243 --> 01:03:53,282
You don't even want me.

1395
01:03:53,282 --> 01:03:55,509
- Hey, I'm not trying to be funny.

1396
01:03:55,509 --> 01:03:57,797
- [Mike] Man, I wish that
were true of Jim Carrey.

1397
01:03:57,797 --> 01:03:59,797
- I was afraid you were.

1398
01:04:03,400 --> 01:04:05,076
- [Tom] "So, can I have your autograph?"

1399
01:04:05,076 --> 01:04:06,681
- Look, Michelle.

1400
01:04:06,681 --> 01:04:09,461
You can't afford to get
mixed up with this bunch.

1401
01:04:09,461 --> 01:04:11,730
- Who says I have to get
mixed up with anyone?

1402
01:04:11,730 --> 01:04:12,719
- [Crow] "I was just lap dancing

1403
01:04:12,719 --> 01:04:15,490
for some old guys, that's all."

1404
01:04:15,490 --> 01:04:18,159
- Listen to me, Michelle.

1405
01:04:18,159 --> 01:04:20,078
The pigs of this world won't
let you sit on the fence

1406
01:04:20,078 --> 01:04:22,249
above the mud and watch
the action for very long.

1407
01:04:22,249 --> 01:04:23,442
- [Mike] They want corn husks.

1408
01:04:23,442 --> 01:04:24,595
- You either run when they spot you,

1409
01:04:24,595 --> 01:04:26,553
or they'll pull you down.

1410
01:04:26,553 --> 01:04:28,636
Then, you have no choice.

1411
01:04:29,699 --> 01:04:31,988
- Now, I say, they have a spot in you,

1412
01:04:31,988 --> 01:04:34,617
and it's time we find a new
fence to straddle for a while.

1413
01:04:34,617 --> 01:04:37,463
- [Crow] Not a chain-link,
though, that would hurt.

1414
01:04:37,463 --> 01:04:40,054
- Just ask me to go away
with you and I will.

1415
01:04:40,054 --> 01:04:43,011
- What in the devil do
you think I've been doing?

1416
01:04:43,011 --> 01:04:45,419
- I mean ask me because you want me.

1417
01:04:45,419 --> 01:04:47,763
Because you need me.

1418
01:04:47,763 --> 01:04:49,213
- Doesn't matter what I want.

1419
01:04:49,213 --> 01:04:50,323
Or need.

1420
01:04:50,323 --> 01:04:51,156
- [Michelle] Critter.

1421
01:04:51,156 --> 01:04:51,989
- [Mike] Where?

1422
01:04:51,989 --> 01:04:52,822
Oh.

1423
01:04:52,822 --> 01:04:55,283
- Please tell me that you love me.

1424
01:04:55,283 --> 01:04:57,697
Then I'll go away with you.

1425
01:04:57,697 --> 01:04:59,505
We can get out of here together.

1426
01:04:59,505 --> 01:05:01,412
- Tell you a thing like that?

1427
01:05:01,412 --> 01:05:05,169
And then have you hate my guts
when you find out about me?

1428
01:05:05,169 --> 01:05:06,157
- [Crow] Her?

1429
01:05:06,157 --> 01:05:08,240
- Not on your life, baby.

1430
01:05:09,619 --> 01:05:11,401
- Find out about what?

1431
01:05:11,401 --> 01:05:12,631
- [Mike] Yeah.

1432
01:05:12,631 --> 01:05:14,177
- Alright.

1433
01:05:14,177 --> 01:05:15,471
You asked for it.

1434
01:05:15,471 --> 01:05:16,590
- [Mike] "I don't like potatoes."

1435
01:05:16,590 --> 01:05:21,157
- You think I'm just a college
dropout from the peace corps.

1436
01:05:21,157 --> 01:05:23,618
Well, I'm much bigger than that.

1437
01:05:23,618 --> 01:05:25,142
- [Mike] "I'm Adolf Hitler."

1438
01:05:25,142 --> 01:05:27,981
- Next week I'll be on the
Wanted list of the FBI.

1439
01:05:27,981 --> 01:05:30,619
Finley Jones, alias Critter Jones.

1440
01:05:30,619 --> 01:05:31,905
- [Crow] Alias Smith and Jones.

1441
01:05:31,905 --> 01:05:33,510
- Wanted for refusal to serve this country

1442
01:05:33,510 --> 01:05:35,504
in the time of a national emergency.

1443
01:05:35,504 --> 01:05:37,274
- Are you supposed to be in the army?

1444
01:05:37,274 --> 01:05:39,788
- Next week I'm supposed
to be, only I won't.

1445
01:05:39,788 --> 01:05:41,305
- A draft dodger.

1446
01:05:41,305 --> 01:05:42,138
You?

1447
01:05:43,029 --> 01:05:44,632
- I don't know.

1448
01:05:44,632 --> 01:05:46,910
All I know is that I gotta
find a hole to crawl into,

1449
01:05:46,910 --> 01:05:48,273
so they can't find me.

1450
01:05:48,273 --> 01:05:49,522
- [Tom] Talk to Courtney Love.

1451
01:05:49,522 --> 01:05:50,870
- [Critter] That's the kind of man I am.

1452
01:05:50,870 --> 01:05:53,248
One that's gotta find
a hole to crawl into.

1453
01:05:53,248 --> 01:05:55,719
- Alright, you'll find your hole.

1454
01:05:55,719 --> 01:05:57,219
(Tom snickers)

1455
01:05:57,219 --> 01:05:59,801
Me, I'm staying here.

1456
01:05:59,801 --> 01:06:01,150
Or should I leave?

1457
01:06:01,150 --> 01:06:04,622
Leo says I'm really going places.

1458
01:06:04,622 --> 01:06:09,335
Just because he deals in
dope, that doesn't tarnish me.

1459
01:06:09,335 --> 01:06:11,907
- Oh, that's what you think, baby.

1460
01:06:11,907 --> 01:06:15,309
Tarnish isn't a strong enough
word for what he'll do to you.

1461
01:06:15,309 --> 01:06:17,229
Try "corrode" for size.

1462
01:06:17,229 --> 01:06:18,443
- [Tom] Yeah, corrode!

1463
01:06:18,443 --> 01:06:19,407
Great!

1464
01:06:19,407 --> 01:06:21,195
- Why don't you take
a good look at Joanie?

1465
01:06:21,195 --> 01:06:23,510
She's been places with Leo.

1466
01:06:23,510 --> 01:06:27,124
And there's a trashy book written
in every line on her face.

1467
01:06:27,124 --> 01:06:28,815
- Aren't you the great one?

1468
01:06:28,815 --> 01:06:29,648
- [Mike] Gretzky?

1469
01:06:29,648 --> 01:06:33,088
- Solving other people's problems.

1470
01:06:33,088 --> 01:06:36,755
- [Crow] "Hey, I polished
my shirt for you!"

1471
01:06:38,086 --> 01:06:41,553
- [Mike] "Bad Traveler, bad boy!"

1472
01:06:41,553 --> 01:06:45,280
- [Tom] So he became a
busker in the London tubes.

1473
01:06:45,280 --> 01:06:48,113
♫ I love her lips

1474
01:06:48,113 --> 01:06:52,070
♫ The touch of her hand

1475
01:06:52,070 --> 01:06:56,237
♫ I love her eyes, the way they shine ♫

1476
01:06:57,851 --> 01:07:02,426
♫ If I could save time in a bottle ♫

1477
01:07:02,426 --> 01:07:06,663
♫ Something inside me makes my heart grow

1478
01:07:06,663 --> 01:07:09,005
- [Tom] One of Morrissey's
more upbeat songs.

1479
01:07:09,005 --> 01:07:12,766
♫ Could be the reason

1480
01:07:12,766 --> 01:07:13,852
- [Mike] I guess he's got a microphone

1481
01:07:13,852 --> 01:07:15,852
implanted in his throat.

1482
01:07:18,543 --> 01:07:20,181
- [Crow] "I can't go out with you,

1483
01:07:20,181 --> 01:07:23,681
